From: jstockdale <jstockdale@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6apm: validate READ/WRITE_DONE payloads by the fields used

Perpetua commit 7c8cc30d7fc4 ("ASoC: qcom: hostless modem voice through
q6apm") added payload-size checks to graph_callback() that reject a
DATA_CMD_RSP_RD/WR_SH_MEM_EP_DATA_BUFFER_DONE_V2 whose payload is
smaller than the full kernel struct. The structs carry trailing
optional metadata words (md_*) that this ADSP firmware does not send:
on the OnePlus Pad 4 every READ_DONE arrives with a 56-byte payload
against sizeof(struct data_cmd_rsp_rd_sh_mem_ep_data_buffer_done_v2)
= 60, so every capture completion is silently dropped — the stream
reaches RUNNING, the DSP fills and reports every buffer (verified by
kprobe: 16/16 packets opcode 0x05001005, tokens 0-7, payload_size 56),
but snd_pcm_period_elapsed() is never called, hw_ptr stays 0 and the
PCM read fails with EIO. The WRITE_DONE path has the same over-strict
check (32-byte struct with md_* tail), killing WCD headphone playback.
Upstream v7.3 has no such check (it only requires ar_graph) and reads
just the leading fields, which is why the Fedora port captures fine.

Keep the NULL-payload and bounds intent but only require the bytes the
handler actually dereferences: buf_addr_msw for READ_DONE and status
for WRITE_DONE (offsetofend). Fixes the denialwm-fleet "capture starts
but no data arrives" regression on iceland/aston/nx809j.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
index 5ea39bd30746..25d3a92589b5 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
@@ -632,7 +632,7 @@ static int graph_callback(const struct gpr_resp_pkt *data, void *priv, int op)
 		break;
 	case DATA_CMD_RSP_WR_SH_MEM_EP_DATA_BUFFER_DONE_V2:
 		if (!graph->ar_graph || !data->payload ||
-		    data->payload_size < (int)sizeof(*done))
+		    data->payload_size < (int)offsetofend(typeof(*done), status))
 			break;
 		client_event = APM_CLIENT_EVENT_DATA_WRITE_DONE;
 		mutex_lock(&graph->lock);
@@ -660,8 +660,13 @@ static int graph_callback(const struct gpr_resp_pkt *data, void *priv, int op)
 
 		break;
 	case DATA_CMD_RSP_RD_SH_MEM_EP_DATA_BUFFER_V2:
+		/*
+		 * The ADSP's READ_DONE omits the trailing metadata words
+		 * (56 bytes here vs the 60-byte struct); only require the
+		 * fields this handler dereferences.
+		 */
 		if (!graph->ar_graph || !data->payload ||
-		    data->payload_size < (int)sizeof(*rd_done))
+		    data->payload_size < (int)offsetofend(typeof(*rd_done), buf_addr_msw))
 			break;
 		client_event = APM_CLIENT_EVENT_DATA_READ_DONE;
 		mutex_lock(&graph->lock);
